bds 6,0 "Heading and speed report"
date 2026-10-14
preamble
    Heading and speed report, magnetic heading, indicated airspeed,
    Mach number and vertical rates from the air data computer.
    Source: ICAO Doc 9871 Table A-2-35.
    Note: signed fields use sign bit + magnitude encoding
    (not two's complement).

items

    HDGSTATUS "Heading Status"
        definition
            Validity of the magnetic heading value.
        element 1
            table
                0: Not valid
                1: Valid

    HDGSIGN "Magnetic Heading Sign"
        definition
            Sign of the magnetic heading magnitude.
        element 1
            table
                0: Positive
                1: Negative
        remark
            Combined with HDG into a single signed value,
            normalised to [0, 360).

    HDG "Magnetic Heading Magnitude"
        definition
            Magnitude of the magnetic heading.
        element 10
            unsigned quantity 90/512 "°"
        remark
            Combined with HDGSIGN into a single signed value.

    IASSTATUS "Indicated Airspeed Status"
        definition
            Validity of the indicated airspeed value.
        element 1
            table
                0: Not valid
                1: Valid

    IAS "Indicated Airspeed"
        definition
            Indicated airspeed.
        element 10
            unsigned quantity 1 "kt"

    MACHSTATUS "Mach Status"
        definition
            Validity of the Mach number value.
        element 1
            table
                0: Not valid
                1: Valid

    MACH "Mach Number"
        definition
            Mach number.
        element 10
            unsigned quantity 1/250 "Mach"

    BARSTATUS "Barometric Vertical Rate Status"
        definition
            Validity of the barometric vertical rate value.
        element 1
            table
                0: Not valid
                1: Valid

    BARSIGN "Barometric Vertical Rate Sign"
        definition
            Sign of the barometric vertical rate magnitude.
        element 1
            table
                0: Positive (climb)
                1: Negative (descent)
        remark
            Combined with BAR into a single signed value.

    BAR "Barometric Vertical Rate Magnitude"
        definition
            Magnitude of the barometric vertical rate.
        element 9
            unsigned quantity 32 "ft/min"
        remark
            Combined with BARSIGN into a single signed value.

    IVVSTATUS "Inertial Vertical Rate Status"
        definition
            Validity of the inertial vertical rate value.
        element 1
            table
                0: Not valid
                1: Valid

    IVVSIGN "Inertial Vertical Rate Sign"
        definition
            Sign of the inertial vertical rate magnitude.
        element 1
            table
                0: Positive (climb)
                1: Negative (descent)
        remark
            Combined with IVV into a single signed value.

    IVV "Inertial Vertical Rate Magnitude"
        definition
            Magnitude of the inertial vertical rate.
        element 9
            unsigned quantity 32 "ft/min"
        remark
            Combined with IVVSIGN into a single signed value.
